{
  "id": "Compound::DB01255 - Gene::6531",
  "verbalization": "Lisdexamfetamine, a central nervous system stimulant, is linked to Slc6a3 through a series of molecular and functional relationships. The evidence suggests that Lisdexamfetamine, which is included in the broader category of Central Nervous System Stimulation, binds to Slc6a2, a protein involved in monoamine transmembrane transport. This interaction implies that Lisdexamfetamine may influence the transport of neurotransmitters across cell membranes, potentially affecting Slc6a3. The shared pathway with Dextroamphetamine, which also binds to Slc6a3, further supports a role for Lisdexamfetamine in modulating monoamine transport. The presence of an ontological link between Lisdexamfetamine and Slc6a3, through the intermediary of Slc6a2, highlights a possible mechanism by which Lisdexamfetamine could influence Slc6a3's function, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
